menu "Twig-oop native drivers"

config DRIVER_CLOCK
    bool "Clock sensor driver (clockdriver)"
    default y
    help
        Periodic clock sensor: posts elapsed-ms-since-boot to the bus every interval.
        Backs the "clock" device in 01.clock.model.

config DRIVER_CONSOLE
    bool "Console output driver (outputdriver)"
    default y
    help
        Serial-console actuator: its write op prints the received value. Backs the
        "console" device in 01.clock.model.

config DRIVER_CELLSET
    bool "CellSet spreadsheet driver (cellsetdriver)"
    default y
    help
        Every Device routed to CellSetDriver is a "cell" holding a plain value or a
        '='-prefixed formula referencing other devices; recalculates on every
        DeviceChanged it depends on. Ported from Java's
        com.peyrona.mingle.controllers.CellSet.

config DRIVER_CRON
    bool "Cron scheduler driver (crondriver)"
    default y
    help
        A Linux-cron-like sensor: one-time or repeating (Daily/Weekly/Monthly/Yearly)
        events, posting the trigger's epoch milliseconds to its Device. Ported from
        Java's com.peyrona.mingle.controllers.Kronos (backed by
        com.peyrona.mingle.lang.japi.Cron).

config DRIVER_SYSMON
    bool "System monitor sensor driver (systemmonitordriver)"
    default y
    select FREERTOS_GENERATE_RUN_TIME_STATS
    help
        Periodically reports one of: EventBus dispatch speed/pending count, CPU load
        (sampled from FreeRTOS's own per-core idle-task run-time counters -- hence this
        option enabling configGENERATE_RUN_TIME_STATS), native heap usage (the "jvmram"
        metric name is kept for .une model compatibility -- there is no JVM here), or a
        constant -1 for the "disk" metric (no filesystem-space API is ported for this
        target). Ported from Java's com.peyrona.mingle.controllers.sysmon.SystemMonitor.

endmenu
